      "interpretation": "Adsorption isotherms for PFOA, PFOS, and GenX on AC and BC-W were obtained in Milli-Q water, groundwater, and two wastewaters after 24 h, and fitted predominantly to Freundlich models (Langmuir for GenX on BC-W). These isotherms quantify sorbed mass per mass of adsorbent as a function of equilibrium concentration for each matrix.",
      "reported_term": "PFAS adsorption isotherms in different water matrices"
    },
    {
      "endpoint_type": "removal",
      "evidence_locator_ids": [
        "S02-E01",
        "S02-E02",
        "S02-E06"
      ],
      "interpretation": "PFAS removal efficiencies were compared across matrices under matched conditions (identical PFAS spikes, adsorbent dose, and contact time). PFAS removal in groundwater remained effective and was similar to or higher than that in Milli-Q water, whereas removal declined in wastewater, especially for PFOA, due to competition from organic matter.",
